lts</h2><p>Keep the selected model, active inputs and units with any result you save or share. A displayed value can change when a different diode assumption, load type or filtering option is selected. Comparing two results is meaningful only when their definitions and operating assumptions agree. Read the methodology for the particular tool instead of assuming that every calculator predicts the same quantity.</p><p>If an input is rejected, review its unit and the supported operating range rather than changing it solely to obtain an accepted result. An accepted calculation is still an estimate under the disclosed assumptions. It is not a test record or a statement that a physical supply meets the needs of your load.</p></div></div></Base>
